1. She is a British VTuber currently in America. (Verbatim: "hi um my name is alias delaria i'm a british vtuber i'm currently in america though")
2. She is from the UK and misses British tea. (Verbatim: "i do miss my british tea i do i do")
3. She has a degree in animal science and a master's in computer science and AI. (Verbatim: "my degree's in animal science and then my master's is in computer science and ai")
4. She replaces swearing with the word "hacking" as a personal quirk. (Verbatim: "i replace i replace it with hacking and that's just that's not a british thing that's just a me thing")
5. She struggles with doing American accents and thinks her attempt is bad. (Verbatim: "my american accent no my american accent's awful it's going to offend so many americans")
6. She plans to return to a schedule of two streams per day once back in England. (Verbatim: "once i'm back in england i should be back to doing two streams a day which i'm very excited for")
7. She identifies as an overworker who works full-time as a VTuber with no set hours. (Verbatim: "i'm an overworking punk so i'm like um i'm i do this full time and i just the problem in doing it full time is there's no set hours you just end up working all the time")
8. She finds it difficult to speak quietly and has been told she is loud during streams. (Verbatim: "i've been told i've been quite loud i'm british yes i'm british")
9. She has visited the Netherlands many times and loves it there. (Verbatim: "i love the netherlands i've visited that's one of the few um places in europe i visited like many many many times")
10. She pronounces certain words differently due to British English, such as "car park" instead of "parking lot" and "bin" instead of "trash can". (Verbatim: "you guys call it parking lot we don't have parking lots in england we call them car parks sidewalk no pavement trash can no bin") [end of text]



1. She has a master's degree in artificial intelligence. (Verbatim: "my master's was in ai yeah that's my fun fact")

2. Before becoming a VTuber, she worked as a software developer. (Verbatim: "before becoming a vtuber i was a software developer yeah yeah software developer yippee")

3. She was planning to pursue a PhD in mathematics, though she disliked the subject. (Verbatim: "technically so i was supposed to go on to do a phd and the phd was in mathematics... i hate maths and that's why i hated physics")

4. Her original accent is from a rural, working-class background, which she describes as a "rough farmer" accent. (Verbatim: "my original accent is that of a farmer is like in former accent it's a rough farmer i grew up rough")

5. She learned Received Pronunciation (RP) accent to pursue TV presenting and to distance herself from her rural roots. (Verbatim: "i really wanted to be doing some form of presenting... you want to learn how to speak with what's it called rp received pronunciation")

6. She grew up in a very working-class ("chavvy") area in the UK. (Verbatim: "i grew up in an extremely chavvy area can confirm like super super super chavvy straight up it was just all chavs")

7. Physics was technically her best academic subject despite her strong dislike for it. (Verbatim: "physics used to be my best subject which is wild because i hated physics the most")

8. She is interested in creating educational content about AI, such as explaining convolutional neural networks. (Verbatim: "i did a stream... where i attempted to explain convolutional neural networks i'm hoping to continue that series")

9. She expresses a desire to learn Morse code in the future. (Verbatim: "my next stream is... just chatting stream where i want to learn morse code just because because why the heck not")

10. She prefers to say "see you later" instead of "goodbye" at the end of streams. (Verbatim: "i don't like bye-byes bye-byes are sad and they suck so i would like to request it be a see you later") [end of text]



1. She has a self-consciousness about her voice and was told in the past it wasn’t suitable for VTubing. (Verbatim: "for those that know i'm quite self-conscious of my voice especially as a vtuber because like i've always been you know there's a lot of times in my past where i've been told that i wouldn't suit vtubing because it's not it's not the right voice")

